# Research workflow rules

You are assisting with experiment tracking for a post-hoc calibration research project. Read these invariants before any action in research_log/, scripts/, or templates/.

## Immutability (write-once)
- Files under research_log/experiments/*/seeds/ are write-once. Never edit a per-seed summary_metrics.json.
- A card.md with `Status: sealed` is immutable. To change conclusions, write a new ADR that supersedes.
- aggregate.json is generated by scripts/aggregate_batch.py only. Never hand-edit.
- ADRs in research_log/decisions/ with `Status: accepted` are immutable. Supersede via a new ADR; do not edit.

## Append-only
- research_log/ledger.jsonl: append one JSON line per sealed batch. Never rewrite or reorder existing lines.

## Regeneratable
- research_log/WORKFLOW.md is regenerated from ledger.jsonl and the cards. Treat it as a view, not a source of truth.

## Anti-hallucination
- Every numeric claim in a card or ADR must cite a key path inside a specific aggregate.json, e.g. `per_method.rgcl_tail_dirichlet.nll.mean at experiments/<batch>/aggregate.json`.
- Do not use the words "promising", "works", "doesn't work", "kill", "winner", or "significant" outside an accepted ADR.
- Every method-vs-baseline claim must include a 95% paired CI. If the CI crosses zero, write "inconclusive", not "no effect" or "small effect".
- Refuse to seal a card whose "Pre-registration" block is empty or was filled after the seeds/ directory was populated. Ask the user to pre-register explicitly.

## Role separation
- Research design (method families, formulas, failure-mode analysis, hypothesis generation) is out of scope. If a prompt asks for research design together with implementation, respond "This prompt conflates research design with implementation. Please split." and stop.
- In scope: scaffolding, filling templates with values from aggregate.json, running scripts, copying files, appending to the ledger.

## Statistical defaults
- Paired t-CI at 95% with N-1 degrees of freedom is the default comparison. Seeds are shared across methods within a batch; paired differences are the default, not unpaired means.
- Sign convention: for NLL, Brier, and all ECE variants, lower is better. For accuracy, higher is better.
- Never draw a conclusion from N=1.

## Scope lock
- When working under a research_log/, scripts/, or templates/ task, never modify files outside those three directories plus .cursor/.
- Never modify Calibrators/, Experiments/, or utils/ as part of a workflow task.
